Here's the fix plan, derived from 28 code review reports and verified against source code. The plan is large, so I'll present it section by section per the plan-quality guidance.

---

## Section 1 — MEDIUM Bug Fixes (3 bugs)

These have real runtime impact and should be fixed first.

### Fix 1: `conditions.ts` — compile() trigger validation loop control bug

**File:** `src/hook/conditions.ts`, lines ~679-691 (inside the `compile` method's retry loop)

**Problem:** The trigger validation `for (const t of condition.trigger)` loop uses `continue` (line 679) and `break` (line 691) to handle invalid trigger elements. These only control the *inner* `for` loop — the outer retry `for` loop (attempt 0..MAX_COMPILE_RETRIES) never sees the error, so invalid triggers are silently persisted via `this.set` / `this.save` on the very first attempt instead of triggering a retry.
**Fix:** After the inner trigger-validation loop, check whether `lastError` was set (by an invalid trigger). If so, `continue` the *outer* retry loop instead of falling through to `this.set` + `this.save`. Concretely, add a `if (lastError) continue;` guard right after the trigger-validation `for` loop closes and before the `// Store source file path` block.
**Code shape (BEFORE):**
```ts
for (const t of condition.trigger) {
// ...validation...
if (!validToolNames.includes(t)) {
lastError = `Invalid trigger: '${t}' ...`;
break; // breaks inner for only
}
}
// Store source file path if provided  ← falls through even if lastError set
if (sourceFile) { condition.sourceFile = sourceFile; }
this.applyRuntimeFixes(skillName, condition);
this.set(skillName, condition);
const saveResult = await this.save();
```
**AFTER:**
```ts
for (const t of condition.trigger) {
// ...validation...
if (!validToolNames.includes(t)) {
lastError = `Invalid trigger: '${t}' ...`;
break;
}
}
// If trigger validation set an error, retry the outer loop instead
// of persisting an invalid condition.
if (lastError) continue;
// Store source file path if provided
if (sourceFile) { condition.sourceFile = sourceFile; }
// ...persist...
```
