I now have all the evidence needed. Let me present the plan.

## Diagnosis Summary

**Root cause**: The WebUI RED "停止" button stays visible because `isRunning` only flips to `false` when the state machine transitions to `prompt`/`await`. Three async operations in the loop are NOT wrapped in `escAware`, so when ESC fires during them, `triggerNeglection()` sets the flag but has no callback to fire — the operation runs to completion (10-30s on a slow endpoint) before the state can reach STOP→PROMPT. During that window, every subsequent click is a no-op because `triggerNeglection()` guards with `if (isNeglectedMode()) return`.

**The three non-escAware blocking operations:**

| # | Location | Operation | Signal available? |
|---|----------|-----------|-------------------|
| 1 | `collect.ts:246` | `checkReactivation()` → bare `forkChat()` | Yes — `forkChat` accepts `signal` as 4th arg, but `undefined` is passed |
| 2 | `collect.ts:458` | `triologue.compact()` after hint-round | Yes — `compact()` accepts `signal` as 2nd arg, but `undefined` is passed |
| 3 | `llm.ts:71` | `triologue.compact()` auto-compact at LLM entry | Same — `undefined` passed for signal |

**Already interruptible (no fix needed):**
- `awaitTeammates()` in STOP — polls `isNeglectedMode()` every 1s → returns `'esc'`
- `runWrapUpLLM()` in esc-wrap-up.ts — runs AFTER STOP→PROMPT, so button is already hidden
- `synthesizeWithSteering()` in prompt.ts — already escAware-wrapped
- Hint-round in collect.ts — already escAware-wrapped
- LLM call, tool execution, crossroad, recap — all already escAware-wrapped

---

## Fix Plan (3 sections)

